# ==============================================================================
# .gitignore for the cc-research-assistant TEMPLATE repo
#
# Philosophy: this repo tracks its full folder structure so forks start with
# a complete scaffold. Almost nothing is actively ignored here.
#
# Downstream projects should UNCOMMENT the sections below to protect data,
# build artifacts, and generated outputs.
# ==============================================================================


# ── Always ignored: OS noise and editor swap files ──
# These are never meaningful content in any repo.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ── Always ignored: Claude Code machine-local settings ──
# settings.local.json contains machine-specific paths and should never be shared.
# Real state files are runtime artifacts; *.example files ARE tracked as scaffolding.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/state/*
!.claude/state/*.example

# ── Always ignored: Claude Code worktrees and personal overrides ──
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/CLAUDE.local.md

# ── Always ignored: Quarto runtime cache ──
# Generated by the Quarto VS Code extension language server even without rendering.
.quarto/

# ── Always ignored: data (Article II — raw and cleaned data never enter git) ──
# Only the .gitkeep placeholders are tracked so forks get the folder structure.
data/raw/**
!data/raw/.gitkeep
data/cleaned/**
!data/cleaned/.gitkeep
data/cache/
# Article II exception: a dataset you built by hand, with no upstream source and no
# licensing restriction, may be committed (git may be its only backup). Whitelist it
# explicitly with a comment naming it, e.g.:
#   !data/cleaned/handcoded_events/
#   !data/cleaned/handcoded_events/**
# Exploration model .rds files can embed restricted data (fixest call_env) — keep them ignored.

# ── Always ignored: secrets and machine-local R config ──
.Rprofile
.env

# ── Always ignored: R / knitr / editor byproducts ──
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
*.RDataTmp
*.Ruserdata
*_cache/
paper/**/*_files/
_freeze/          # Quarto freeze cache (execute: freeze: auto); regenerated on render
.luarc.json


# ==============================================================================
# ── Add in downstream projects ──
# None of the blocks below apply to the template itself. Uncomment after forking.
# ==============================================================================

# ── LaTeX build artifacts ──
# *.aux
# *.bbl
# *.blg
# *.fdb_latexmk
# *.fls
# *.log
# *.nav
# *.out
# *.snm
# *.toc
# *.vrb
# *.synctex.gz
# *.run.xml
# *-blx.bib

# ── Compiled PDFs ──
# *.pdf

# ── Python cache ──
# __pycache__/
# *.pyc
# *.pyo

# ── R session files ──
# .Rhistory
# .RData
# .Rdata
# .Rproj.user/

# ── IDE project files (optional — some teams track these) ──
# .vscode/
# .idea/

# ── Quarto / LaTeX compilation outputs ──
# /.quarto/
# paper/.quarto/
# paper/quarto/*_files/
# paper/quarto/.quarto/
# _output/

# ── Generated HTML reports ──
# project_dashboard.html
# research_overview.html
# quality_reports/**/*.html

# ── Built documentation site ──
# docs/

/.quarto/
**/*.quarto_ipynb
/_output/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Quarto keep-tex output (audited by scripts/paper_coherence.py and verify.py; regenerated on render)
paper/main.tex
paper/appendix.tex
/paper/sections/*.tex

/.luarc.json
